    "P:cursor-monotonicity-rebase-and-atomic-checkpoints"
  ],
  "context": {
    "client_id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-c10000000001",
    "notes": [
      "step 4 moves row e1 from this user's bucket to another owner's (owner_id → user-b): the server records a tombstone for the bucket value the row left at seq 2, before the moved row at seq 3, in the same commit (D-bucket-move-out)",
      "the step-5 pull names only the old bucket: it receives the tombstone and not the moved row, which is outside its bucket and the invoker's RLS scope, and the cursor advances past seq 3 because it tracks the global sequence horizon, not delivered rows (P:keyset-pagination-and-delivery-bound)",
      "the tombstone removes e1 in the local transaction that commits the page and the cursor, so a device that pulls only the old bucket keeps no copy of a row that left it (P:cursor-monotonicity-rebase-and-atomic-checkpoints)"
    ],
